","lic":"CC BY 2.5","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.5","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%C4%8Cvarci.jpg"}},"dish/dahibara-aloodum":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/dahibara-aloodum","n":"Dahibara Aloodum","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish found in 2 cuisines","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Dahibara Aloodum is a popular street food originating from Cuttack of the state Odisha. It is a variant of Dahi vada. The dish is prepared by soaking vadas (fried flour balls) in light dahi (yogurt) water which is tempered with mustard seeds and curry leaves. Then adding Aludum (potato curry) and Ghuguni (pea curry) to it, topped with an assortment of spices, onions, and coriander."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-dahibara-aloodum"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dahibara_Aloodum"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Odia cuisine","cuisine/odia-cuisine"],["Oriya cuisine","cuisine/oriya-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":4,"links":[["Dahi (curd)","ingredient/dahi-curd"],["Dahi vada","ingredient/dahi-vada"],["Potato","ingredient/potato"],["Vada","ingredient/vada"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Away in the Kitchen (Odia home cooking)","ref":"site/awayinthekitchen-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"awayinthekitchen.com","note":"Blog section devoted to Odia home recipes.","url":"https://www.awayinthekitchen.com/odia-home-cooking","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"Archana's Kitchen (Oriya)","ref":"site/archanaskitchen-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"archanaskitchen.com","note":"Odia cuisine section of Archana Doshi's large Indian recipe site.","url":"https://archanaskitchen.com/cuisine/oriya","suggested":true,"kind":"site"},{"name":"Away in the Kitchen (Odia home cooking)","ref":"site/awayinthekitchen-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"awayinthekitchen.com","note":"Blog section devoted to Odia home recipes.","url":"https://www.awayinthekit