"ingredient/noodle","n":"Noodle","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 11 dishes across 10 cuisines","intro":[["Noodles are a type of food typically made from unleavened dough which is rolled flat and cut, stretched, or extruded into long strips or strings. Noodles are a staple food in many cultures and made into a variety of shapes. The most common noodles are those derived from Chinese cuisine or Italian cuisine. Italian noodles are generally referred to as pasta. In Chinese cuisine, the overarching term for noodles is 麵 (miàn in Mandarin), which refers specifically to dough-based noodles made from wheat or other grain-based dough. Chinese noodles also include another category, called 粉 (fěn), which are not made by kneading dough but from a starch slurry, such as rice noodles (mǐfěn, 米粉), and cellophane noodles (fěnsī, 粉丝 / 粉絲). These are not made from wheat dough, but are still regarded as noodles in English due to their physical form and culinary role."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-noodle"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Noodle"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":10,"groups":[["Indonesian cuisine","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine",[["Mie ayam","dish/mie-ayam"],["Mie caluk","dish/mie-caluk"],["Mie celor","dish/mie-celor"],["Mie kocok","dish/mie-kocok"]]],["South Korean cuisine","cuisine/south-korean-cuisine",[["Jjolmyeon","dish/jjolmyeon"],["Milmyeon","dish/milmyeon"]]],["Acehnese cuisine","cuisine/acehnese-cuisine",[["Mie caluk","dish/mie-caluk"]]],["Belarusian cuisine","cuisine/belarusian-cuisine",[["Zatiruha","dish/zatiruha"]]],["Kazakh cuisine","cuisine/kazakh-cuisine",[["Naryn (dish)","dish/naryn-dish"]]],["Korean Chinese cuisine","cuisine/korean-chinese-cuisine",[["Ulmyeon","dish/ulmyeon"]]],["Kyrgyz cuisine","cuisine/kyrgyz-cuisine",[["Naryn (dish)","dish/naryn-dish"]]],["North Korean cuisine","cuisine/north-korean-cuisine",[["Pyongyang Raengmyon","di